    <string name="about_title">About</string>
    <string name="about_application_section">About this app</string>
    <string name="about_application_description">Photo Organizer indexes photos and videos on this device, then helps you review them with keep and discard marks. Discarded items are only removed after Android displays its system confirmation.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_description">Indexing, review marks and media tools stay on the device. Media tools create a new file and do not overwrite the original.</string>
    <string name="about_features_section">What it does</string>
    <string name="about_feature_index_title">On-device index</string>
    <string name="about_feature_index_summary">Scans the Images and Video collections, then reports counts, size and which folders they came from. The scan is cancellable and re-runs when the permission grant changes.</string>
    <string name="about_feature_modes_title">Three review modes</string>
    <string name="about_feature_modes_summary">Smart mode queues by likely payoff — duplicates first, then screenshots, then large files. Targeted mode filters by album, date range, type and minimum size. Manual mode is a date-grouped grid with batch selection.</string>
    <string name="about_feature_duplicates_title">Duplicates and look-alikes</string>
    <string name="about_feature_duplicates_summary">Exact duplicates are found by SHA-256 over the whole file, so a rename cannot hide one. Look-alikes use a perceptual hash to catch burst shots and re-encodes; that pass is opt-in because it decodes every image.</string>
    <string name="about_feature_cleanup_title">Screenshots and large files</string>
    <string name="about_feature_cleanup_summary">Both are listed with a running total of what deleting them would free. The large-file threshold is selectable between 5 and 100 MB.</string>
    <string name="about_feature_processing_title">Local media processing</string>
    <string name="about_feature_processing_summary">Images convert to JPEG, WebP or PNG with a long-edge limit, a quality target and optional Exif. Videos convert to 1080p, 720p or 480p with a chosen codec and bitrate ceiling, or hand back only their audio. A result larger than its source is discarded automatically. Every result waits in a temporary folder until you have compared it against its source, and only then is it written back beside the original.</string>
    <string name="about_feature_privacy_title">No network, no overwrites</string>
    <string name="about_feature_privacy_summary">The app declares no internet permission, so nothing can leave the device. Source files are never modified — processing writes a new file — and deletion always goes through Android\'s own confirmation dialog.</string>
    <string name="about_open_source_section">Source code and licenses</string>
    <string name="about_license_note">The listed projects retain their own copyright notices and license terms. Transitive dependencies are grouped under the project that brings them in.</string>
    <!-- Page help -->
    <string name="help_action_cd">Page help</string>
    <string name="dashboard_help_title">About the dashboard</string>
    <string name="dashboard_help_message">This page answers one question: where does the library stand. It reports how many photos and videos are indexed, how much space they take, how much of the library you have reviewed, and how much could be reclaimed.\n\nPull down, or use the refresh button, to scan again after adding or deleting files. Nothing here changes a file — the cards are shortcuts into review and cleanup.</string>
    <string name="organize_help_title">About organizing</string>
    <string name="organize_help_message">Choose how to walk through the library. Smart mode queues the likely wins first: duplicates, then screenshots, then large files. Targeted mode filters by album, date range, type and minimum size before you start. Manual mode is a date-grouped grid with batch selection.\n\nKeep and discard are only marks. Discarded items collect under Discarded and are removed only when you ask for it, after Android shows its own confirmation.</string>
    <string name="review_help_title">About quick review</string>
    <string name="review_help_message">One item at a time, and every decision can be changed later. Swipe right to keep, swipe left to discard, or use the three buttons under the preview. Swipe up or down to move to the next or previous item without deciding.\n\nAlbum files the item into a logical album, which groups it inside this app without moving the file on disk. Tap the preview to open it full screen. Marks can be revisited in the Kept and Discarded lists.</string>
    <string name="grid_help_title">About this grid</string>
    <string name="grid_help_message">%1$s\n\nTap a tile to open it full screen, or press and hold to peek. To act on several items, use the select button in the top bar and tap the tiles you want — the toolbar that appears carries the actions this list supports. The search button filters by file name, and the strip along the right edge jumps through the list by date.</string>
    <string name="grid_help_scope_manual">Every indexed item, grouped by capture date.</string>
    <string name="grid_help_scope_kept">The items you marked as kept. Clearing a mark returns an item to the un-reviewed pool.</string>
    <string name="grid_help_scope_trash">The items you marked as discarded. They are still on the device: deleting them is a separate step and Android asks for confirmation first.</string>
    <string name="grid_help_scope_screenshots">Screenshots only, recognised from the folder and file name.</string>
    <string name="grid_help_scope_largest">Only files above the threshold set on the Tools page.</string>
    <string name="grid_help_scope_duplicate_group">One group of copies. Keeping one and discarding the rest is the point of this view; the group was matched by content, not by name.</string>
    <string name="grid_help_scope_album">One logical album. The grouping exists inside this app — on disk the files stay where they are.</string>
    <string name="grid_help_scope_processing">The files you pick here are re-encoded with the settings on the previous page. Nothing is written to your gallery until you have compared the results.</string>
    <string name="tools_help_title">About tools</string>
    <string name="tools_help_message">Two kinds of tool. Cleanup analysis looks for exact duplicates (SHA-256 over the whole file), look-alikes (a perceptual hash of the picture, started on demand because it decodes every image), screenshots, and files above a threshold you pick. Media processing re-encodes photos and videos with the device\'s own codecs.\n\nAnalysis only reads. Nothing is deleted without a mark and a system confirmation.</string>
    <string name="media_tools_help_title">About media tools</string>
    <string name="media_tools_help_message">Re-encode photos and videos on this device. Pick the output settings first, then choose the files: they are processed one after another, and a result that ends up larger than its source is dropped.\n\nResults are staged in a temporary folder so you can compare each one against its source. What you approve is copied back into the folder the source came from, under the source\'s own name plus a -z1 suffix that counts the compression passes. The original is never modified or replaced, and deleting it is a separate question asked at the end.</string>
    <string name="tools_duplicate_help_title">About exact duplicates</string>
    <string name="tools_duplicate_help_message">Each group holds files whose contents are byte-identical, matched with SHA-256 over the whole file, so a rename or a different folder cannot hide one. Keep one marks every other copy in that group as discarded, and the menu in the top bar applies the same strategy to all groups at once.\n\nNothing is deleted here: the marks land in the Discarded list.</string>
    <string name="tools_similar_help_title">About look-alikes</string>
    <string name="tools_similar_help_message">Each group holds pictures that look alike without being the same file: burst shots, re-encodes, resized copies. They are matched by a perceptual hash of the picture, so confirm a group before acting on it — the copies differ in quality or size, and which one to keep is a judgement call.\n\nKeeping one marks the rest as discarded; deletion is still a separate, confirmed step.</string>
    <string name="settings_help_title">About settings</string>
    <string name="settings_help_message">Theme, review behaviour, and the defaults the media tools open with. Index range decides which albums are scanned at all, which is the quickest way to keep an album out of every review task.\n\nUpdates are the one part of the app that uses the network, and it is off until you turn it on. Everything else works with no connection at all.\n\nEvery page in the app carries this help button; it explains what that page is for and how its controls behave.</string>

